const gallery = images && images.length > 1 ? images : undefined;

// Cascading slide-0 fallback — see `primaryImageFallbacks`'s own JSDoc. 2026-09-09, extended
// (provisionally — Marcel's own framing: build it, then decide keep-or-lose) to cover gallery
// mode too: a live defect on product `4673TS251` showed this was needed for exactly the case
// that matters most — a multi-image product whose first photo is the one that's broken.
// **Which candidate list slide 0 cascades through depends on whether a gallery is active:**
// with a gallery, it cascades through the gallery's OWN sequence (`gallery` itself) — if
// `images[0]` fails, slide 0 shows `images[1]` instead, staying self-consistent with what the
// rest of the gallery already shows, rather than jumping to the unrelated `primaryImage` (which
